apply the marketing principles by critically analyzing real-world marketing scenarios.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall, Spring.", "catalogComments": "Similar in content to M.B.A. core course NCC 5030. This course can be used to fulfill a core course in the Undergraduate Business Minor.", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "Enrollment limited to: non-Johnson School students.", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "GM", "acadGroup": "BU", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2811, "crseId": 350814, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "NCC", "catalogNbr": "5560", "titleShort": "Managerial Finance", "titleLong": "Managerial Finance", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 9121, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "08:05AM", "timeEnd": "09:20AM", "startDt": "01/24/2022", "endDt": "05/10/2022", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 36, "netid": "ym355", "firstName": "Yifei", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Mao"}], "pattern": "TR", "facilityDescr": "Baker Laboratory 335", "bldgDescr": "Baker Laboratory", "facilityDescrshort": "BKL335", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "Enrollment limited to non-Johnson Graduate and UG Seniors/Juniors Only.\nUG Sophomores by Permission Only.\nNon-Johnson Students ONLY:  January 18th at 8:00am to February 7th at 11:59pm.  You may add or drop a full semester class after February 7th with permission of the faculty. A late fee of $100.00 will be charged for each add or drop transaction. If you are dropping after March 21st at11:59pm you will also receive a \"W\" on your transcript in addition to the late fees.\nThere will be no enrollment from a wait list into a class if you have a time conflict or if it will create an overload."}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "01/24/2022", "endDt": "05/21/2022", "addConsent": "I", "addConsentDescr": "Instructor Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "O", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 3, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "GRI", "gradingBasisShort": "GradeNoAud", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only (no audit)", "simpleCombinations": [{"subject": "HADM", "catalogNbr": "2250", "type": "W"}], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/24/2022", "sessionEndDt": "05/21/2022", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "This course provides an introduction to business finance through lectures and assignments. The content of the course varies with the section and instructor. Topics may include basic financial accounting, time value of money, stock and bond valuation, capital budgeting, portfolio theory, asset-pricing models, cost of capital, dealing with risk, capital structure, acquisitions, and options. Application of theory to practical applications will be stressed in the lectures.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "Forbidden Overlap: due to an overlap in content, students will not receive credit for both\u00a0HADM 2220\u00a0and NCC 5560.\n\u00a0", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall, Spring.", "catalogComments": "This course is similar in content to MBA\u00a0core course NCC 5060. Please note: undergraduate students\u00a0may be limited to which section they can enroll in.\u00a0Graduate students have first priority in the event the course is oversubscribed.", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "Prerequisite: instructors of some sections may require a previous course in financial accounting.\u00a0", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "Enrollment limited to: non-Johnson School graduate students, seniors and juniors.", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "GM", "acadGroup": "BU", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2811, "crseId": 350815, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "NCC", "catalogNbr": "5580", "titleShort": "Managing Operations", "titleLong": "Managing Operations", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 9138, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "02:55PM", "timeEnd": "04:10PM", "startDt": "01/24/2022", "endDt": "05/10/2022", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 19, "netid": "nst43", "firstName": "Natalia", "middleName": "", "lastName": "Santamaria"}], "pattern": "MW", "facilityDescr": "Sage Graduate Hall B05", "bldgDescr": "Sage Hall", "facilityDescrshort": "SGHB05", "meetingTopicDescription": ""}], "notes": [{"classNotesSeq": 1, "descrlong": "Enrollment limited to non-Johnson Graduate and UG Seniors Only.\nNon-Johnson Students ONLY:  January 18th at 8:00am to February 7th at 11:59pm.  You may add or drop a full semester class after February 7th with permission of the faculty. A late fee of $100.00 will be charged for each add or drop transaction. If you are dropping after March 21st at11:59pm you will also receive a \"W\" on your transcript in addition to the late fees.\nThere will be no enrollment from a wait list into a class if you have a time conflict or if it will create an overload."}], "campus": "MAIN", "campusDescr": "Ithaca", "location": "ITH", "locationDescr": "Ithaca, NY (Main Campus)", "startDt": "01/24/2022", "endDt": "05/21/2022", "addConsent": "D", "addConsentDescr": "Department Consent Required", "isComponentGraded": true, "crseAttrs": [], "instructionMode": "P", "instrModeDescrshort": "In Person", "instrModeDescr": "In Person", "topicDescription": "", "openStatus": "C", "exploreCriteriaIds": [], "materials": []}], "unitsMinimum": 3, "unitsMaximum": 3, "componentsOptional": [], "componentsRequired": ["LEC"], "gradingBasis": "GRI", "gradingBasisShort": "GradeNoAud", "gradingBasisLong": "Letter grades only (no audit)", "simpleCombinations": [], "sessionCode": "1", "sessionBeginDt": "01/24/2022", "sessionEndDt": "05/21/2022", "sessionLong": "Regular Academic Session", "exploreCriteriaIds": []}], "description": "Operations Management is the design and management of processes that transform inputs into finished goods or services. All organizations have operations that directly affect their ability to execute on their specified strategies. This course prepares students to think analytically and managerially about operations processes, and to use the tools and intuition they acquire to ensure that the operations in production and service systems support the business strategies for these systems. A process view of operations will be used to analyze different key operational dimensions such as flow time management, service operations management, quality management, inventory management and supply chain management.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Spring.", "catalogComments": "Similar in content to M.B.A. core course NCC 5080.", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "Enrollment limited to: non-Johnson School students.", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "GM", "acadGroup": "BU", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}]}, "message": null, "meta": {"copyright": "Cornell University, Office of the University Registrar", "rosterDttm": "2022-06-10T07:44:21-0400", "catalogDttm": "2022-06-09T19:14:04-0400"}}